node_modules/
# ...and any SIDECAR COPY of it. `node_modules/` matches that exact name only, so
# a repair/rollback backup like `node_modules.bak.wi5769/` is NOT ignored — and
# git-sync auto-commits the whole tree, so one such directory tries to push
# ~100k files and trips the GitHub 100MB blob limit (observed 2026-07-25: a
# concurrent-install repair left node_modules.bak.wi5769/, and git-sync had to
# exclude @cloudflare/workerd's 118MB binary from the auto-commit). Taking a
# backup before a risky reinstall is the RIGHT instinct — this just makes it safe.
node_modules.bak*/
node_modules.old*/

# Python bytecode generated by hook syntax/compile checks and runtime imports.
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc

.next/
.next-prod/
.next-build-cache/

# Vitest scratch TMPDIR. Agents + the green-checkpoint run vitest with
# TMPDIR=$PWD/.vitest-tmp (the documented ENOENT workaround when the real TMPDIR
# is unwritable). Those are throwaway temp + node-compile-cache files — never
# source. Tracking them churned 8500+ junk files into the shared tree, spawned
# noise "should not commit" auto-commits, and slowed git-sync (WI-679). Ignore
# everywhere they land (root, packages/*, apps/*).
.vitest-tmp/
**/.vitest-tmp/

# Claude/Node compile-cache scratch.  The Codex/Claude hooks may place a
# node-compile-cache under a repository-local `.tmp-claude/`; it is generated
# binary/cache data, never source.  Leaving it visible makes git-sync sweep the
# cache and can trip the secret scanner on embedded npm documentation strings
# that merely look like PEM material (P-302 / WI-1326481).
.tmp-claude/
**/.tmp-claude/
# The content-fixer writes repository-local V8 compile-cache artifacts while
# repairing generated docs. They are disposable binary output, never source;
# ignoring both root and nested roots keeps git-sync and source lints from
# treating them as shippable files.
.content-fixer-tmp/
**/.content-fixer-tmp/
# Node's repository-local compile cache is disposable machine-specific output,
# not source. Ignore both root and nested Papercusp temp roots so git-sync does
# not sweep it into commits or guarded-build source fingerprints.
.papercusp-tmp/
**/.papercusp-tmp/

# These repository-root names are reserved for agent/test scratch. Keep the
# rules root-anchored so legitimate nested source directories with similar
# names remain visible. Existing tracked files still need index-only removal.
/.agent-tmp
/.tmp
/.tmp-*
/.tsx-tmp
/scratch
/scratchpad
/scratch-*
