# ignored, but the ROOT lockfile is the npm-ci source of truth for CI +
# fresh clones (regenerated + validated 2026-06-11, audit P-024/EI-84) —
# ignoring it meant CI had no lockfile and `npm ci` could never run.
package-lock.json
!/package-lock.json
*.tsbuildinfo
.DS_Store
*.log
!docs/evidence/shared-agent-obligations-2026-09-07-acceptance-tests.log
!docs/evidence/shared-agent-obligations-2026-09-07-recovery-tests.log
!docs/evidence/shared-agent-obligations-2026-09-07-launch-injection-tests.log
!docs/evidence/shared-agent-obligations-2026-09-07-launch-current-tests.log

# Vitest coverage output (published as CI artifacts, never committed — spec §1.13)
# coverage-*/ variants (EI-22195215129102176): a non-default --coverage.reportsDirectory
# (e.g. comparing two coverage configs) is otherwise NOT ignored, and git-sync sweeps it
# into a commit within ~1 minute with git status reading clean afterwards.
coverage/
coverage-*/
**/coverage/
**/coverage-*/
# ...but `coverage-census/` is SOURCE, not coverage output (2026-09-02). The
# **/coverage-*/ pattern above silently swallowed every NEW file added to
# packages/operator-core/lib/coverage-census/ — invisible to `git status`, never
# staged, never swept by git-sync. Its 24 pre-existing files survived only because
# gitignore does not affect already-TRACKED files, so the directory looked healthy
# while being closed to additions. Two files written for WI-2142121 stranded on
# disk for ~15min before this was caught; the work-item's completion could not
# settle past `proposed` because its filesChanged were missing-from-commit.
!**/coverage-census/

# Per-run test output (p2p-perf bench artifacts + report.md, Playwright, etc.).
# Ephemeral, keyed by a timestamp/runId — NOT source. Committed baselines that
# ARE source live elsewhere (e.g. perf/baselines/*.json) and are unaffected.
# (2026-06-07: git-sync was sweeping p2p-perf run dirs into commits.)
test-results/
**/test-results/
.env
.env.local
# Cloudflare wrangler local secrets (JWT_SECRET, CF tokens). Was tracked until
# 2026-09-30 (open-source-release P-013); never commit it again.
**/.dev.vars
.source/

# Rust/Tauri build artifacts — accidentally committed before; never again.
# (2026-06-05: apps/{tui,pui-zellij-plugin,pui-companion-proto}/target/ got swept
# into git-sync commits — 10GB of unpushed >100MB blobs wedged the push for 20h.)
apps/*/target/
apps/operator-mobile/src-tauri/target/
# per-work-item isolated cargo target dirs (CARGO_TARGET_DIR=.wiNNNN-cargo-target):
# 2026-07-09 git-sync excluded a 240MB blob from .wi3388-cargo-target/ every sweep
.wi*-cargo-target/
*cargo-target*/
# Sidecar backup dirs left by desktop packaging (2026-07-10: git-sync excluded a
# 100.1MB node binary from papercusp-desktop/src-tauri/sidecar.old.55111/ every
# sweep — same class as the cargo-target churn above; never source).
sidecar.old*/
**/sidecar.old*/

# operator-docs (Astro+Starlight)
apps/operator-docs/dist/
apps/operator-docs/.astro/
# DOCS_PREVIEW (P-005 projection site): preview build out-dir + the generated
# lib-API markdown starlight-typedoc writes into the content tree. Both are
# projected from code on demand — never committed.
apps/operator-docs/dist-preview/
apps/operator-docs/src/content/docs/preview/

# papercusp-docs (Astro+Starlight)
apps/papercusp-docs/dist/
apps/papercusp-docs/.astro/

# Repo-root Astro prerender cache. Its generated modules contain checkout-specific
# absolute source IDs and are runtime build output, not repository content.
/.astro/

# src-as-entry packages — `build` (tsc) emits dist/, but package.json "exports"
# routes every subpath to ./src/*, so nothing ever consumes the emitted dist/.
#
# Tracking it is worse than useless. The copy goes stale and starts CONTRADICTING
# src: agent-mcp/dist/_bulk.js sat 13 days behind and kept teaching the hard-coded
# `ok: true` envelope that src/_bulk.ts had already replaced with `ok: failed === 0`
# — the exact false-success contract that removal was meant to retire (WI-10002064).
# A grep or an agent reading the tracked artifact gets re-taught the removed rule.
#
# Adding a rule here is only HALF the fix: a tracked path is never ignored, so the
# rule goes inert unless the path is also untracked (`git rm -r --cached <path>`).
# Guard against the next one: `npm run lint:no-tracked-src-entry-dist`.
#
# ⚠ ONLY superproject paths belong in this block. `packages/tooldef/dist/` and
# `packages/tooldef-http/dist/` used to be listed here and were DEAD rules by
# 2026-09-20: both packages had moved to submodules (libs/generic/tooldef,
# libs/generic/tooldef-http) and neither `packages/` path existed any more. Worse
# than useless — a reader grepping this file saw "tooldef-http/dist is ignored" and
# moved on while libs/generic/tooldef-http/dist/ sat committed. A superproject rule
# cannot reach inside a submodule even when the path IS right, so those rules live
# in each submodule's own .gitignore (same reach gap as WI-4419 / EI-22201289307647151).
packages/tooldef-mcp/dist/
packages/agent-mcp/dist/

# Per-spawn MCP config written into a harness cwd by console-launch /
# bootstrap-role (SU + role sessions). For the `papercup` harness that cwd IS
# this main checkout, and the file carries a SIGNED, time-limited MCP URL — it
# must never be committed (paperclip's `git add -A` would otherwise leak the
# credential). Was historically tracked then deleted; this closes the re-leak
# hole. `.papercusp.bak` is the backup console-launch makes of a pre-existing one.
.mcp.json
.mcp.json.papercusp.bak

# Rendered plan markdown — plans are PG-canonical; these .md are a DERIVED,
# read-only projection (rendered by `plans:export` for human reading), never the
# source of truth. Tracking them is the PG-mirror anti-pattern + constant churn
# (293 plans × many agents editing = a .md diff on every plan edit). Edits go via
# the plans tools, not these files. (2026-06-06: a full `plans:export --toDir`
# materialized all 293; this keeps them local-and-readable but out of git.)
apps/operator/docs/plans/**/*.md

# On-demand generated API projections (docs-and-memory-as-projections P-004):
# NOT committed by design — they cold-import the full tool registry / re-doc
# every lib export, so a committed copy churns on every tool or export change
# fleet-wide. Regenerate with `npm run gen:openapi` / `npm run gen:lib-api`.
.papercusp/openapi.json
.papercusp/lib-api/

# Gate-owned frozen-candidate repair worktrees are linked checkouts, never source.
# Without this rule git-sync's blanket add records the checkout itself as a mode-160000
# gitlink. The next candidate then inherits that undeclared gitlink and recursive git
# commands fail with "No url found ... in .gitmodules" (WI-39450).
.papercusp/worktrees/

# WI-42354 (2026-08-27): the dependency-generation store is host-local RUNTIME state —
# generation trees plus .pins/ lease heartbeats that dependency-generation.sh rewrites
# (updated=<epoch>) on EVERY gate materialization. While tracked, git-sync committed that
# heartbeat bump hourly, moving every pot's tip with zero real changes and permanently
# defeating the gate's up-to-date short-circuit. Nothing reads this store from git
# history (dependency-generation.sh reads the live fs only). Nested form per WI-4419:
# slash-anchored patterns miss the .papercusp dirs that appear inside packages/apps.
.papercusp/dependency-generations/
**/.papercusp/dependency-generations/
# The env-named generation store recorded for env-less callers (WI-10005159).
**/.papercusp/dependency-generation-root

# git-sync-embedded-repo-strand fix (2026-06-30, joint w/ 2b1a8 / WI-1354): transient test-scratch
# dirs that get a nested .git (an embedded repo). When ANY has NO commit checked out, `git add -A`
# FATALs (exit 128) → stages nothing → the whole tree strands uncommitted silently. Ignore ALL the
# tmp roots the lockdom/flg-repo/green-checkpoint/commit-reproject tests use in-repo. (git-sync also
# now excludes-and-retries on the fatal — run-git-sync.ts — so this is defense-in-depth.)
.vitest-tmp/
.vitest-tmpdir/
**/.vitest-tmp/
**/.vitest-tmpdir/
**/vitest-tmp/
.papercusp/vitest-tmp/
.papercusp/scratch/
**/scratch/relgit-*/
**/scratch/lockdom-*/

# WI-4419 (2026-07-12): a gitignore pattern containing a slash is ANCHORED to the
# directory of the .gitignore holding it — so `.papercusp/scratch/` above matches
# ONLY <repo-root>/.papercusp/scratch/. Agent state dirs also appear NESTED
# (packages/operator-core/.papercusp/, apps/operator/.papercusp/, ...), where the
# anchored patterns miss them — and git-sync auto-commits the whole tree, so what
# the pattern misses is committed automatically. That is how 529 scratch files and
# a live hyperbee LevelDB (whose LOG embeds the build box's home path + hostname)
# came to be TRACKED, and thence swept into every release bundle by the sidecar glob.
# These `**/` twins are the depth-matching guard (same fix already applied to
# .vitest-tmp above). Untracking what is ALREADY committed is separate — see WI-4419.
**/.papercusp/scratch/
**/.papercusp/vitest-tmp/
**/.papercusp/tmp/
**/.papercusp/tmp-*
**/.papercusp/node-compile-cache
**/.papercusp/tsx-*
**/.papercusp/logs/
**/.papercusp/bench-reports/
**/.papercusp/pi-sessions/

# EI-19319605650500051 (2026-08-30): a LEADING DOT is what agents already reach for to
# mean "scratch, deleted after this run" — and that intent counts for nothing here,
# because git-sync auto-commits the whole tree on a schedule. The file is committed
# before the agent gets back to deleting it. Measured, not hypothetical:
# `agent-tools/coordination/.wi1347-live-verify.test.ts` opened with the words
# "THROWAWAY (not committed, deleted after run)", was committed anyway, survived ~a
# week, and became a genuine shared-gate red (harness_shared.test_runs source='ci',
# 5 failures, latest 2026-08-02T05:37:44Z) — while INSERTing and DELETEing rows in the
# LIVE fleet coordination tables (coord_presence, event_awaits) from what the runner
# treats as a unit test. These patterns make the leading dot actually hold.
#
# ⚠ Do NOT "fix" the related glob inconsistency by making the runner match dotfiles.
# vitest's include glob runs tinyglobby with dot:false, so a dot-prefixed test is not
# collected by a normal run (measured 2026-08-30: pattern
# `**/*.{test,spec}.?(c|m)[jt]s?(x)` returns nothing for `.scratch.test.ts`, and
# returns it under dot:true). Two consequences, and they point the same way: a
# dot-prefixed file is ALREADY broken as a real test — it silently never runs — and it
# is still reachable by an explicitly-named invocation, which is how the gate came to
# run the file above. Setting dot:true would make the gate START collecting scratch,
# which is backwards. The fix is to stop it being committed, which is this pattern.
**/.*.test.ts
**/.*.test.tsx
**/.*.test.mts
**/.*.test.cts
**/.*.spec.ts
**/.*.spec.tsx

# Dependency-generation publishers stage an in-progress tree under a
# `.build-pending-*` directory. It is a disposable runtime sentinel, not a
# generation artifact; git-sync's whole-tree add must never publish it while a
# build overlaps a sync tick.
.papercusp/dependency-generations/.build-pending-*/
**/.papercusp/dependency-generations/.build-pending-*/

# EI-21895919268589129 (2026-08-30): the `hive-fromrepo` smoke test snapshots a
# WHOLE REPO COPY — including a ~100.7MB `bin/node` binary — into the tree and
# does not clean up. Measured while git-sync freshness sat DEGRADED with 4 missed
# 3-minute intervals (nothing committed fleet-wide for ~14 minutes): 486 of the
# 496 dirty paths (98%) were this one abandoned 4.5GB directory, last written 4h
# earlier. Its `bin/node` also exceeds the 95MB per-file limit, so every single
# sweep re-hit the oversize-exclusion path on the same file.
#
# This is the THIRD instance of one failure mode — see the ~100.1MB node binary
# from `sidecar.old.55111/` noted above, and WI-2911's 1.85GB below. Ignoring
# directories one at a time after the fact treats the symptom; the durable fix is
# for the smoke runner to snapshot OUTSIDE the repo. This pattern is the stopgap
# that keeps git-sync's cadence from collapsing until it does.
#
# NOTE: gitignore never untracks. 5804 files / 245.8MB of this directory were
# already committed into HEAD by an earlier sweep; removing those from the index
# is a separate deliberate call, tracked on EI-21895919268589129 (WI-2911 is the
# precedent for the index-only untrack).
.papercusp-smoke-snapshots/
**/.papercusp-smoke-snapshots/

# npm-only repo — a pnpm/yarn install breaks the shared node_modules layout (2026-07-03 fleet incident)
pnpm-lock.yaml
yarn.lock
.pnpm-workspace-state-v1.json

# WI-2911 (2026-07-05): ~1.85GB of never-source content was tracked into the shared
# tree — the bulk of `git archive HEAD` and of the release seed bundle. Untracked
# index-only (files stay on disk); these entries keep it from re-entering.
# Agent scratch/temp under .papercusp (scratch/ + vitest-tmp/ already ignored above).
.papercusp/tmp/
.papercusp/tmp-*/

# EI-22169218440134434: belt-and-braces for any script that still defaults its output
# dir to a bare repo-root tmp/ (e.g. an old cache, a manual run) — anchored to the repo
# root so it can never match a legitimate nested tmp/ inside a package (e.g.
# some-package/src/tmp/ source content).
/tmp/
.papercusp/logs/
.papercusp/bench-reports/
.papercusp/pi-sessions/
